-- 교수진 상세 페이지 통일 (2026-11-07). 김형준 교수 페이지 구조를 기준으로 국문/영문을 같은 틀로 맞춘다.
--   약력: 학력 → 경력 → (주요 수상) → (학회 활동) → 주요 논문 / Education → Experience → Selected Awards → Professional Service → Selected Publications
--   연구 소개: 국문 페이지는 국문, 영문 페이지는 영문. 「주제 제목<br>본문」 형식.
-- 내용은 지금 사이트에 있는 것을 그대로 옮기고 정리만 했다(새 사실을 더하지 않음). 논문 목록은 그대로.
-- 이미 같은 틀로 정리된 이종석·강문성·류재건·박제영 교수와 석학교수(최정우)는 건드리지 않는다.

-- 이성현
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과·바이오융합기술 2014 공학사</li><li>서강대학교 화학과 2020 이학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>기초과학연구원 유전체교정연구단 선임연구원 (2020–2022)</li><li>기초과학연구원 유전체교정연구단 연구위원(팀 리더) (2022)</li><li>엣진(Edgene Inc.) 수석연구원(연구개발팀장) (2022–2023)</li><li>성균관대학교 의과대학 메타바이오헬스학과 조교수·부교수 (2023–2026)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 부교수 (2026–현재)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Kim S, Kim J, Cha S, et al. “In vivo mitochondrial base editing restores genotype and visual function in a mouse model of LHON.” Nature Communications. 2025;16:10923.</li><li>Kim S, Park SG, Kim J, et al. “Comprehensive phenotypic assessment of mitochondrial ND5 nonsense mutation in mice.” Experimental and Molecular Medicine. 2024;56:2395-2408.</li><li>Cho SI, Lim K, Hong S, et al. “Engineering TALE-linked deaminases to facilitate precision adenine base editing in mitochondrial DNA.” Cell. 2024;187:95-109.e26.</li><li>Lee S, Lee H, Baek G, Kim JS. “Precision mitochondrial DNA editing with high-fidelity DddA-derived base editors.” Nature Biotechnology. 2023;41:378-386.</li><li>Lee S, Lee H, Baek G, et al. “Enhanced mitochondrial DNA editing in mice using nuclear-exported TALE-linked deaminases and nucleases.” Genome Biology. 2022;23:211.</li><li>Cho SI, Lee S, Mok YG, et al. “Targeted A-to-G base editing in human mitochondrial DNA with programmable deaminases.” Cell. 2022;185:1764-1776.e12</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering and Bio-Convergence Technology, Sogang University (2014)</li><li>Ph.D., Chemistry, Sogang University (2020)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Senior Researcher, Center for Genome Engineering, Institute for Basic Science (2020–2022)</li><li>Research Fellow (Team Leader), Center for Genome Engineering, Institute for Basic Science (2022)</li><li>Principal Researcher (Head of R&amp;D), Edgene Inc. (2022–2023)</li><li>Assistant/Associate Professor, Department of MetaBioHealth, Sungkyunkwan University School of Medicine (2023–2026)</li><li>Associate Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2026–present)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Kim S, Kim J, Cha S, et al. “In vivo mitochondrial base editing restores genotype and visual function in a mouse model of LHON.” Nature Communications. 2025;16:10923.</li><li>Kim S, Park SG, Kim J, et al. “Comprehensive phenotypic assessment of mitochondrial ND5 nonsense mutation in mice.” Experimental and Molecular Medicine. 2024;56:2395-2408.</li><li>Cho SI, Lim K, Hong S, et al. “Engineering TALE-linked deaminases to facilitate precision adenine base editing in mitochondrial DNA.” Cell. 2024;187:95-109.e26.</li><li>Lee S, Lee H, Baek G, Kim JS. “Precision mitochondrial DNA editing with high-fidelity DddA-derived base editors.” Nature Biotechnology. 2023;41:378-386.</li><li>Lee S, Lee H, Baek G, et al. “Enhanced mitochondrial DNA editing in mice using nuclear-exported TALE-linked deaminases and nucleases.” Genome Biology. 2022;23:211.</li><li>Cho SI, Lee S, Mok YG, et al. “Targeted A-to-G base editing in human mitochondrial DNA with programmable deaminases.” Cell. 2022;185:1764-1776.e12</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>저희 연구실은 화공생명공학, 유전체 교정, 미토콘드리아 생물학이 만나는 지점에서 연구합니다. 단백질, 유전체, 미토콘드리아, 세포를 공학적으로 설계할 수 있는 생물 시스템으로 보고, 새로운 틀로 그 기능을 제어하고 최적화합니다.</p><p>유전체 교정 단백질 공학<br>분자 수준에서는 프로그래밍 가능한 유전체 교정 단백질을 설계하고, 그 활성과 특이성, 전달 효율을 최적화합니다.</p><p>미토콘드리아 유전체 교정과 질환 모델<br>세포 수준에서는 미토콘드리아 유전체를 정밀하게 교정하고, 유전적 변화가 이형질성(heteroplasmy), 세포 대사, 질환 표현형에 미치는 영향을 정량적으로 연구합니다. 이 결과를 유전질환 모델, 치료용 유전체 교정 전략, 그리고 의료·산업용으로 기능이 개선된 세포 시스템으로 확장합니다.</p><p>분자 진단과 공학 세포 분석<br>질환 진단과 공학 세포의 품질 평가를 위한 분자 검출·기능 분석 기술도 개발합니다. 분자 설계, 세포 공정 공학, 정량 분석, 치료 효능 검증을 통합해 미토콘드리아 질환을 비롯한 인간 질환을 위한 확장 가능한 생물공학 플랫폼을 구축하고자 합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Our research lies at the interface of chemical and biomolecular engineering, genome editing, and mitochondrial biology. We view proteins, genomes, mitochondria, and cells as engineerable biological systems and apply a novel framework to control and optimize their functions.</p><p>Genome-Editing Protein Engineering<br>At the molecular level, we engineer programmable genome-editing proteins and optimize their activity, specificity, and delivery.</p><p>Mitochondrial Genome Editing and Disease Models<br>At the cellular level, we precisely modify mitochondrial genomes and quantitatively investigate how genetic alterations affect heteroplasmy, cellular metabolism, and disease phenotypes. These findings are further translated into genetic disease models, therapeutic genome-editing strategies, and engineered cell systems with improved functions for biomedical and industrial applications.</p><p>Molecular Diagnostics and Engineered-Cell Analysis<br>We also develop molecular detection and functional analysis technologies for disease diagnosis and the quality assessment of engineered cells. By integrating molecular design, cellular process engineering, quantitative characterization, and therapeutic validation, we aim to establish scalable bioengineering platforms for mitochondrial disorders and other human diseases.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '이성현';

-- 오세용
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 1986 공학사</li><li>University of Tsukuba 1989 공학석사</li><li>University of Tsukuba 1993 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 교수 (1994–현재)</li><li>Cornell University(미국)·동경공업대학(일본) 방문교수</li></ul><h3>학회 활동</h3><ul><li>한국공업화학회 편집이사·재무이사</li><li>한국고분자학회 평이사</li><li>한국에너지기술평가원 고급에너지 인력양성사업 단장</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Ga-Eun Lee, Joo Hwan Kim, Jinyoung Kim, Hyun-Seok Cho, Simon MoonGeun Jung, Yuichiro Hayashi, Toshiaki Ito, Kohei Yamaguchi, Yuta Saegusa, Hideaki Takahashi, Hiroshi Sato, Tsutomu Miyasaka, Gyu Min Kim, Se Young Oh, "Interfacial engineering with a carbonyl-functionalized truxene self-assembled monolayer for high efficiency and stable NiOX-based perovskite solar cells." Chemical Engineering Journal (2026): 176106.</li><li>Jinyoung Kim, Joo Hwan Kim, Hyun-Seok Cho, Gyu Min Kim, Se Young Oh, "Mechanochemical All-in-Powder Strategy with Intrinsic Additive Incorporation for High-Efficiency and Durable Perovskite Solar Cells" Small (2025), 21.52: e09799.</li><li>Seri Lee, Gyu Min Kim, Tsutomu Miyasaka, Dong-Il Won, Se Young Oh, "Ge-doped Sn-Pb assisted by MACl triple metal cation perovskite solar cells with high open-circuit voltage" Chemical Engineering Journal (2024), 488: 150817.</li><li>Chan Hyuk Ji, Seon-ju Lee, Se-Young Oh, "P3HT-based visible-light organic photodetectors using PEI/PAA multilayers as a p-type buffer layer", RSC advances (2019) 9.64: 37180-37187.</li><li>Seong Bin Lim, Chan Hyuk Ji, Il Soo Oh, Se-Young Oh, "Reduced leakage current and improved performance of an organic photodetector using an ytterbium cathode interlayer", Journal of Materials Chemistry C (2016) 4.22: 4920-4926.</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Sogang University (1986)</li><li>M.S., University of Tsukuba (1989)</li><li>Ph.D., University of Tsukuba (1993)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (1994–present)</li><li>Visiting Professor, Cornell University (USA) and Tokyo Institute of Technology (Japan)</li></ul><h3>Professional Service</h3><ul><li>Editorial Director and Financial Director, Korean Society of Industrial and Engineering Chemistry</li><li>Board Member, The Polymer Society of Korea</li><li>Director, Advanced Energy Human Resources Development Program, Korea Institute of Energy Technology Evaluation and Planning</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Ga-Eun Lee, Joo Hwan Kim, Jinyoung Kim, Hyun-Seok Cho, Simon MoonGeun Jung, Yuichiro Hayashi, Toshiaki Ito, Kohei Yamaguchi, Yuta Saegusa, Hideaki Takahashi, Hiroshi Sato, Tsutomu Miyasaka, Gyu Min Kim, Se Young Oh, "Interfacial engineering with a carbonyl-functionalized truxene self-assembled monolayer for high efficiency and stable NiOX-based perovskite solar cells." Chemical Engineering Journal (2026): 176106.</li><li>Jinyoung Kim, Joo Hwan Kim, Hyun-Seok Cho, Gyu Min Kim, Se Young Oh, "Mechanochemical All-in-Powder Strategy with Intrinsic Additive Incorporation for High-Efficiency and Durable Perovskite Solar Cells" Small (2025), 21.52: e09799.</li><li>Seri Lee, Gyu Min Kim, Tsutomu Miyasaka, Dong-Il Won, Se Young Oh, "Ge-doped Sn-Pb assisted by MACl triple metal cation perovskite solar cells with high open-circuit voltage" Chemical Engineering Journal (2024), 488: 150817.</li><li>Chan Hyuk Ji, Seon-ju Lee, Se-Young Oh, "P3HT-based visible-light organic photodetectors using PEI/PAA multilayers as a p-type buffer layer", RSC advances (2019) 9.64: 37180-37187.</li><li>Seong Bin Lim, Chan Hyuk Ji, Il Soo Oh, Se-Young Oh, "Reduced leakage current and improved performance of an organic photodetector using an ytterbium cathode interlayer", Journal of Materials Chemistry C (2016) 4.22: 4920-4926.</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>고효율·고안정성 페로브스카이트 태양전지<br>유무기 하이브리드, 전무기, 무연(lead-free) 페로브스카이트를 이용한 태양전지를 개발합니다. 새로운 계면 공학 기술로 전하 운반체를 제어하는 연구를 중심으로, 높은 효율과 안정성을 갖춘 페로브스카이트 태양전지의 구현과 상용화를 목표로 합니다.</p><p>유기 기반 광전지와 광검출기<br>유무기 하이브리드 광활성층과 전하 전달 버퍼층을 이용한 유기 전자소자를 연구합니다. 고효율 유기 전자소자를 만들기 위해 임피던스 기법으로 미세 계면의 전기적 특성을 분석하고, 광전 변환 효율에 영향을 주는 나노구조의 특징을 연구합니다. 또한 Ag 투명전극, 유연 기판, 새로운 버퍼층을 이용한 유연 유기 태양전지와 광검출기를 개발합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Highly Efficient and Stable Perovskite Solar Cells<br>We develop solar cells based on organic–inorganic hybrid, all-inorganic, and lead-free perovskites. Our main focus is carrier management through new interface-engineering techniques, toward perovskite solar cells with high efficiency and stability and their commercialization.</p><p>Organic-Based Photovoltaic Cells and Photodetectors<br>We study organic electronic devices that use organic–inorganic hybrid photoactive layers and charge-transfer buffer layers. To fabricate high-efficiency organic electronic devices, we examine the electrical characteristics of micro-interfaces by impedance techniques and the features of nanostructures that affect photoelectric conversion efficiency. We also develop flexible organic solar cells and photodetectors using Ag transparent electrodes, flexible substrates, and novel buffer layers.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '오세용';

-- 최진훈
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 1988 공학사</li><li>University of Missouri-Rolla 1990 공학석사</li><li>UCLA 1993 이학석사</li><li>UCLA 1996 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 교수 (1997–현재)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Bomje Woo, Donggyun Shin, Daeryook Yang, Jinhoon Choi, “Reduced model and simulation of neuron with passive dendritic cable: An eigenfunction expansion approach”, Journal of Computational Neuroscience, 19 (2005) 379-397.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, Kwang Soon Lee “Mixed Constrained Infinite Horizon Linear Quadratic Optimal Control”, Asian Journal of Control, 9 (2003) 412-418.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, Wook Hyun Kwon, “Continuity and Exponential Stability of Mixed Constrained Model Predictive Control”, SIAM Journal on Control and Optimization, 42 (2003) 839-870.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, “On the Stabilization of Linear Discrete Time Systems Subject to Input Saturation”, Systems and Control Letters, 36 (1999) 241-244.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, “Connections Between Local Stability in Lyapunov and Input/Output Senses”, IEEE Tracsactions on Automatic Control, 40 (1995) 2139-2143.</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Sogang University (1988)</li><li>M.S., University of Missouri-Rolla (1990)</li><li>M.S., UCLA (1993)</li><li>Ph.D., UCLA (1996)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (1997–present)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Bomje Woo, Donggyun Shin, Daeryook Yang, Jinhoon Choi, “Reduced model and simulation of neuron with passive dendritic cable: An eigenfunction expansion approach”, Journal of Computational Neuroscience, 19 (2005) 379-397.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, Kwang Soon Lee “Mixed Constrained Infinite Horizon Linear Quadratic Optimal Control”, Asian Journal of Control, 9 (2003) 412-418.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, Wook Hyun Kwon, “Continuity and Exponential Stability of Mixed Constrained Model Predictive Control”, SIAM Journal on Control and Optimization, 42 (2003) 839-870.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, “On the Stabilization of Linear Discrete Time Systems Subject to Input Saturation”, Systems and Control Letters, 36 (1999) 241-244.</li><li>Jinhoon Choi, “Connections Between Local Stability in Lyapunov and Input/Output Senses”, IEEE Tracsactions on Automatic Control, 40 (1995) 2139-2143.</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>뇌는 사람과 동물의 행동을 결정하는 지능의 중심입니다. 뇌는 여러 감각기관에서 들어오는 실시간 신호를 평생 학습한 경험과 통합해 판단합니다. 생물학적 지능을 이해하려면 뇌가 정보를 어떻게 처리하는지 알아야 합니다. 브레인포매틱스(Brainformatics)는 뇌가 정보를 어떻게 부호화하고 처리하는지 이해하는 연구 분야입니다. 저희는 신경망으로 나타나는 지능의 시스템 수준 계산신경과학과, 의사결정·게임 이론의 개인 수준 행동경제학을 주로 연구합니다.</p><p>계산신경과학<br>연상기억: 연상기억은 아리스토텔레스가 처음 제안한 개념입니다. 이론적·계산적 도구로 뇌에서 연상기억이 어떻게 저장되고, 떠올려지고, 소실되는지 연구합니다. 지각의 다양체(manifold) 방식: 물체의 위치, 크기, 방향, 거리에 관계없이 같은 물체로 지각하게 하는 원리도 연구합니다.</p><p>행동경제학<br>상대적 의사결정 이론: 신고전 경제학은 인간이 합리적이라고 가정해 의사결정의 심리를 배제했습니다. 그러나 사람은 감정 등 여러 요인의 영향을 받아 합리적이지 않은 경우가 많습니다. 전망 이론, 후회 이론 등 여러 기술적(descriptive) 모형이 제안되었지만 다양한 비합리적 행동을 설명하는 데 한계가 있습니다. 저희는 기존 모형보다 더 많은 현상을 설명하는 새로운 의사결정 이론을 만들고자 합니다. 게임 이론: 존 내시가 제안한 내시 균형은 게임 이론의 핵심 도구이고, 진화 게임 이론에서는 학습을 통한 전략의 진화를 다루는 진화적 안정 균형이 제안되었습니다. 두 개념은 같지 않으며, 저희는 둘을 아우르는 새로운 이론을 개발하고자 합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>The brain is the intelligence center of humans and animals that decides their behaviors. It integrates real-time sensory signals from various sensory organs with experiences learned throughout life. To understand biological intelligence, we need to know how the brain processes information. Brainformatics is the area of research that seeks to understand how the brain encodes and processes information. The brain is studied at levels ranging from the molecular to the social; we mainly study system-level computational neuroscience of intelligence manifested through neural networks, and individual-level behavioral economics of decision and game theories.</p><p>Computational Neuroscience<br>Associative memory: the associative memory was first proposed by Aristotle. We try to understand how associative memories are stored, recalled, and degraded in the brain using theoretical and computational tools. Manifold ways of perception: we also study the problem of manifold ways of perception that allows position-, size-, direction-, and distance-invariant perception of objects.</p><p>Behavioral Economics<br>Relative decision theory: neoclassical economics ignored the psychology of decision by assuming that humans are rational, to obtain a normative theory. However, there are many cases where humans are not rational but are affected by factors such as emotions. Many descriptive decision models have been proposed, including prospect theory and regret theory, but all have limitations in explaining various non-rational behaviors. We aim to develop a new theory of decision making that can explain more than other models. Game theory: the Nash equilibrium proposed by John Nash is the central tool of game theory, while evolutionary game theory proposes the evolutionarily stable equilibrium, in which game strategies evolve through learning. The two concepts are not equivalent, and we aim to develop a new theory that encompasses both.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '최진훈';

-- 이진원
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>Carnegie Mellon University 1993 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>University of Virginia 연구원 (1993–1994)</li><li>광운대학교 교수 (1994–2005)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Sukhyeong Cho, Yun Seo Lee, Hanyu Chai, Sang Eun Lim, Jeong Geol Na, Jinwon Lee, “Enhanced production of ectoine from methane using metabolically engineered Methylomicrobium alcaliphilum 20Z”, Biotechnol Biofuels 15, 5(2022)</li><li>Gyo-Yeon Seo, Hoe-Suk Lee, Hyeonsoo Kim, Sukhyeong Cho, Jeong-Geol Na, Young Joo Yeon, Jinwon Lee, “A novel hyperthermophilic methylglyoxal synthase: molecular dynamic analysis on the regional fluctuations”, Sci Rep 11, 2538 (2021)</li><li>Sukhyeong Cho, Seonyoung Ha, Hye Su Kim, Jin Hee Han, Hyeonsoo Kim, Young Joo Yeon, Jeong Geol Na, Jinwon Lee, “Stimulation of cell growth by addition of tungsten in batch culture of a methanotrophic bacterium, Methylomicrobium alcaliphilum 20Z on methane and methanol”, Journal of Biotechnology, 309 (2020), 0168-1656</li><li>Jeongmo Yang, Ji Hee Son, Hyeonsoo Kim, Sukhyeong Cho, Jeong-geol Na, Young Joo Yeon, Jinwon Lee, “Mevalonate production from ethanol by direct conversion through acetyl-CoA using recombinant Pseudomonas putida, a novel biocatalyst for terpenoid production”, Microb Cell Fact 18, 168 (2019)</li><li>Hyeonsoo Kim, Jeongmo Yang, Sukhyeong Cho, Kijun Jeong, Jinbyung Park, Jinwon Lee, “Microbial synthesis of undec-9-enoic acid, heptyl ester from renewable fatty acids using recombinant Corynebacterium glutamicum-based whole-cell biocatalyst”, Process Biochemistry, 66 (2018), 1359-5113</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>Ph.D., Carnegie Mellon University (1993)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Research Associate, University of Virginia (1993–1994)</li><li>Professor, Kwangwoon University (1994–2005)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Sukhyeong Cho, Yun Seo Lee, Hanyu Chai, Sang Eun Lim, Jeong Geol Na, Jinwon Lee, “Enhanced production of ectoine from methane using metabolically engineered Methylomicrobium alcaliphilum 20Z”, Biotechnol Biofuels 15, 5(2022)</li><li>Gyo-Yeon Seo, Hoe-Suk Lee, Hyeonsoo Kim, Sukhyeong Cho, Jeong-Geol Na, Young Joo Yeon, Jinwon Lee, “A novel hyperthermophilic methylglyoxal synthase: molecular dynamic analysis on the regional fluctuations”, Sci Rep 11, 2538 (2021)</li><li>Sukhyeong Cho, Seonyoung Ha, Hye Su Kim, Jin Hee Han, Hyeonsoo Kim, Young Joo Yeon, Jeong Geol Na, Jinwon Lee, “Stimulation of cell growth by addition of tungsten in batch culture of a methanotrophic bacterium, Methylomicrobium alcaliphilum 20Z on methane and methanol”, Journal of Biotechnology, 309 (2020), 0168-1656</li><li>Jeongmo Yang, Ji Hee Son, Hyeonsoo Kim, Sukhyeong Cho, Jeong-geol Na, Young Joo Yeon, Jinwon Lee, “Mevalonate production from ethanol by direct conversion through acetyl-CoA using recombinant Pseudomonas putida, a novel biocatalyst for terpenoid production”, Microb Cell Fact 18, 168 (2019)</li><li>Hyeonsoo Kim, Jeongmo Yang, Sukhyeong Cho, Kijun Jeong, Jinbyung Park, Jinwon Lee, “Microbial synthesis of undec-9-enoic acid, heptyl ester from renewable fatty acids using recombinant Corynebacterium glutamicum-based whole-cell biocatalyst”, Process Biochemistry, 66 (2018), 1359-5113</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>C1 가스의 생물학적 유용 화학물질 전환<br>C1 가스는 지구온난화를 일으키는 대표적인 온실가스이지만, 탄소를 더해 새로운 탄소 사슬을 만들면 재생 가능한 자원이 될 수 있습니다. 기존의 C1 가스 활용 기술은 고온·고압의 여러 공정이 필요해 석유 대비 경제성이 낮다는 문제가 있습니다. 저희 연구실은 생촉매를 이용해 저온·저압에서 C1 가스를 직접 전환하는 것을 목표로 합니다. 메탄, 일산화탄소 같은 C1 가스를 유용한 화학물질로 전환하는 미생물 생촉매를 개발하며, 유전공학을 이용한 C1 가스 전환 미생물의 탐색과 개량, 그리고 용해도가 낮은 C1 가스를 효율적으로 전환하기 위한 생물공정을 연구합니다. 추가 생물전환을 통해 고부가가치 바이오화학물질로 전환하는 연구도 진행합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Biological Conversion of C1 Gas to Useful Chemicals<br>C1 gases are representative greenhouse gases that cause global warming, but adding carbons to C1 gas creates new carbon chains that can serve as a renewable resource. Existing technologies that use C1 gas have low economic feasibility compared with petroleum because they require various processes at high temperature and pressure. Our laboratory aims instead to use biocatalysts to convert C1 gas directly at low temperature and pressure. We develop microbial biocatalysts that convert C1 gases (methane, carbon monoxide) into useful chemicals, focusing on the isolation (screening) and improvement of capable microorganisms by genetic engineering and on bioprocesses for efficient conversion of poorly soluble C1 gas. We also convert these products into high-value biochemicals through additional bioconversion.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '이진원';

-- 오병근
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 1995 공학사</li><li>서강대학교 1997 공학석사</li><li>서강대학교 2003 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>Northwestern University 박사후연구원 (2004–2006)</li><li>Auburn University 방문교수 (2012)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Myeong-Jun Lee, Eun-Sol Lee, Tae-Hwan Kim, Ju-Won Jeon, YongTae Kim, Byung-Keun Oh, “Detection of thioredoxin-1 using ultra-sensitive ELISA with enzyme-encapsulated human serum albumin nanoparticle”, Nano Convergence 6 (2019) 1-7.</li><li>Jinho Yoon, Taek Lee, Jinhee Jo, Byung-Keun Oh, Jeong-Woo Choi, “Electrochemical H2O2 biosensor composed of myoglobin on MoS2 nanoparticle-graphene oxide hybrid structure”, Biosensors and Bioelectronics 93 (2017) 14-20.</li><li>Jin-Ha Choi, Hai-Jin Hwang, Seung Won Shin, Jeong-Woo Choi, Soong Ho Um, Byung-Keun Oh, “A novel albumin nanocomplex containing both small interfering RNA and gold nanorods for synergetic anticancer therapy” Nanoscale 7 (2015) 9229-9237.</li><li>Jin-Ha Choi, Han Kim, Jae-Hak Choi, Jeong-Woo Choi, Byung-Keun Oh. “Signal Enhancement of Silicon Nanowire-Based Biosensor for Detection of Matrix Metalloproteinase-2 Using DNA-Au Nanoparticle Complexes” ACS applied materials &amp; interfaces 5 (2013) 12023-12028.</li><li>Jin Ha Choi, Hyun Soo Kim, Jeong-Woo Choi, Jong Wook Hong, Young-Kee Kim, Byung-Keun Oh, “A novel Au-nanoparticle biosensor for the rapid and simple detection of PSA using a sequence-specific peptide cleavage reaction” Biosensors and Bioelectronics 49 (2013) 415-419.</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Sogang University (1995)</li><li>M.S., Sogang University (1997)</li><li>Ph.D., Sogang University (2003)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Postdoctoral Fellow, Northwestern University (2004–2006)</li><li>Visiting Professor, Auburn University (2012)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Myeong-Jun Lee, Eun-Sol Lee, Tae-Hwan Kim, Ju-Won Jeon, YongTae Kim, Byung-Keun Oh, “Detection of thioredoxin-1 using ultra-sensitive ELISA with enzyme-encapsulated human serum albumin nanoparticle”, Nano Convergence 6 (2019) 1-7.</li><li>Jinho Yoon, Taek Lee, Jinhee Jo, Byung-Keun Oh, Jeong-Woo Choi, “Electrochemical H2O2 biosensor composed of myoglobin on MoS2 nanoparticle-graphene oxide hybrid structure”, Biosensors and Bioelectronics 93 (2017) 14-20.</li><li>Jin-Ha Choi, Hai-Jin Hwang, Seung Won Shin, Jeong-Woo Choi, Soong Ho Um, Byung-Keun Oh, “A novel albumin nanocomplex containing both small interfering RNA and gold nanorods for synergetic anticancer therapy” Nanoscale 7 (2015) 9229-9237.</li><li>Jin-Ha Choi, Han Kim, Jae-Hak Choi, Jeong-Woo Choi, Byung-Keun Oh. “Signal Enhancement of Silicon Nanowire-Based Biosensor for Detection of Matrix Metalloproteinase-2 Using DNA-Au Nanoparticle Complexes” ACS applied materials &amp; interfaces 5 (2013) 12023-12028.</li><li>Jin Ha Choi, Hyun Soo Kim, Jeong-Woo Choi, Jong Wook Hong, Young-Kee Kim, Byung-Keun Oh, “A novel Au-nanoparticle biosensor for the rapid and simple detection of PSA using a sequence-specific peptide cleavage reaction” Biosensors and Bioelectronics 49 (2013) 415-419.</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>현장진단(POCT)을 위한 바이오센서 플랫폼 기술<br>미세유체 기술 기반의 바이오센서 플랫폼은 필요한 장치를 모두 담아 휴대하기 쉽고 사용이 간편한 소형 기기입니다. 이 기기로 환자 진료 현장이나 환경 시료 채취 현장에서 바로 검사(POCT)할 수 있고, 빠른 결과로 의료 현장의 진료를 개선할 수 있습니다. 저희 연구실은 현장에서 검사할 수 있는 신속 항원 진단·신속 분자 진단 기기의 플랫폼 기술을 개발합니다.</p><p>기능성 나노바이오 소재<br>최근 다기능성을 갖춘 생체소재 기반 나노입자가 큰 주목을 받고 있습니다. 나노바이오 소재는 특성을 세밀하게 조절하기 쉬워 생명공학 응용에 적합합니다. 저희 연구실은 환경·의료 바이오센싱 등 다양한 응용을 위한 새로운 나노구조 소재를 설계·제조하며, 특히 고감도 바이오센서 개발에 응용하는 데 집중합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Biosensor Platform Technology for Point-of-Care Testing<br>A microfluidics-based biosensor platform is a compact device with all necessary instrumentation in a portable, easy-to-use format. Such devices enable point-of-care testing (POCT) at patient-care or environmental sampling sites, and their rapid results can improve patient care. Our laboratory develops platform technologies for rapid antigen and rapid molecular diagnostic devices capable of on-site examination.</p><p>Functional Nano-Bio Materials<br>In recent years, biomaterial-based nanoparticles with multifunctional properties have received a great deal of attention. The ease of fine-tuning nano-biomaterials makes them strong candidates for biotechnology applications. Our laboratory designs and manufactures novel nanostructured materials for a wide range of applications, including environmental and medical biosensing, with a particular focus on highly sensitive biosensors.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '오병근';

-- 강태욱
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서울대학교 2001 공학사</li><li>서울대학교 2006 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>University of California, Berkeley 방문연구원 (2014–2015)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 교수 (2017–현재)</li><li>서강대학교 화공생명공학과 학과장 (2017–2019)</li><li>서강대학교 통합바이오연구소 소장 (2019–현재)</li></ul><h3>학회 활동</h3><ul><li>Scientific Reports (Nature Publishing Group) 편집위원 (2015–현재)</li><li>한국화학공학회 이사 (2016–현재)</li><li>한국화학공학회 NICE 편집위원 (2016–현재)</li><li>한국바이오칩학회 학술위원 (2016–현재)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Yuseung Jo et al., Inner membrane-bound gold nanoparticles as efficient electron transfer mediators for enhanced mitochondrial electron transport chain activity, Nano Letters (2022)</li><li>Keumrai Whang et al., Direct and Precise Determination of Volumetric Mass Transfer Coefficient of Carbon Monoxide for Miniaturized Gas-liquid Reactors via Sensitive Probing of Raman Transitions, Chemical Engineering Journal, 429, 132260 (2022)</li><li>Keumrai Whang et al., Water-wettable Open Plasmonic Nanocavities for Ultrasensitive Molecular Detections in Multiple Phases, Nano Letters, 21 (14), pp 6194-6201 (2021)</li><li>Yonghee Shin et al., Microfluidic Multi-scale Homogeneous Mixing with Uniform Residence Time Distribution for Rapid Production of Various Metal Core–shell Nanoparticles, Advanced Functional Materials, 31, 202007856 (2021)</li><li>Jeehan Chang et al., "Generalized On-demand Production of Nanoparticle Monolayers on Arbitrary Solid Surfaces via Capillarity-Mediated Inverse Transfer, Nano Letters, 19 (3), pp 2074-2083 (2019)</li><li>Jin-Ho Lee et al., General and Programmable Synthesis of Hybrid Liposome/metal Nanoparticles, Science Advances, 2, e1601838 (2016)</li><li>Kihoon Kim et al., Interfacial liquid-state surface-enhanced Raman spectroscopy, Nature Communications, 4, 2182 (2013)</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Seoul National University (2001)</li><li>Ph.D., Seoul National University (2006)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Visiting Scholar, University of California, Berkeley (2014–2015)</li><li>Professor, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2017–present)</li><li>Chair, Department of Chemical and Biomolecular Engineering, Sogang University (2017–2019)</li><li>Director, Institute of Integrated Biotechnology, Sogang University (2019–present)</li></ul><h3>Professional Service</h3><ul><li>Editorial Board Member, Scientific Reports (Nature Publishing Group) (2015–present)</li><li>Trustee, The Korean Institute of Chemical Engineers (2016–present)</li><li>Editor, NICE, The Korean Institute of Chemical Engineers (2016–present)</li><li>Academic Board, The Korean BioChip Society (2016–present)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Yuseung Jo et al., Inner membrane-bound gold nanoparticles as efficient electron transfer mediators for enhanced mitochondrial electron transport chain activity, Nano Letters (2022)</li><li>Keumrai Whang et al., Direct and Precise Determination of Volumetric Mass Transfer Coefficient of Carbon Monoxide for Miniaturized Gas-liquid Reactors via Sensitive Probing of Raman Transitions, Chemical Engineering Journal, 429, 132260 (2022)</li><li>Keumrai Whang et al., Water-wettable Open Plasmonic Nanocavities for Ultrasensitive Molecular Detections in Multiple Phases, Nano Letters, 21 (14), pp 6194-6201 (2021)</li><li>Yonghee Shin et al., Microfluidic Multi-scale Homogeneous Mixing with Uniform Residence Time Distribution for Rapid Production of Various Metal Core–shell Nanoparticles, Advanced Functional Materials, 31, 202007856 (2021)</li><li>Jeehan Chang et al., "Generalized On-demand Production of Nanoparticle Monolayers on Arbitrary Solid Surfaces via Capillarity-Mediated Inverse Transfer, Nano Letters, 19 (3), pp 2074-2083 (2019)</li><li>Jin-Ho Lee et al., General and Programmable Synthesis of Hybrid Liposome/metal Nanoparticles, Science Advances, 2, e1601838 (2016)</li><li>Kihoon Kim et al., Interfacial liquid-state surface-enhanced Raman spectroscopy, Nature Communications, 4, 2182 (2013)</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>플라즈모닉 센서와 광유체 통합 플랫폼을 이용한 혁신 진단·환경 모니터링<br>나노플라즈모닉 센서는 뛰어난 감지 성능으로 큰 관심을 받고 있습니다. 저희는 균일한 플라즈모닉 나노구조를 통합한 새로운 광유체(optofluidic) 플랫폼을 개발해 다양한 센싱에 응용합니다. 예를 들어 플라즈모닉 나노구조의 빠른 광-열 변환을 이용한 광학 중합효소연쇄반응(PCR)으로 표적 유전자를 초고속 증폭하는 차세대 광유체 분자진단 칩을 개발하고 있으며, 복잡한 환경에서 다양한 생체 분자를 현장에서 고감도로 모니터링하는 광유체 센싱 플랫폼도 연구합니다.</p><p>무기 메타물질과의 계면을 이용한 인공 생체소재 개발과 의생명 응용<br>생체 구성 요소의 핵심 기능을 모사하거나 강화한 인공 생체소재를 합리적으로 설계·합성합니다. 예를 들어 미토콘드리아의 전자전달계(ETC)는 미토콘드리아 기능 유지에 필수적이지만, 미토콘드리아 DNA 돌연변이나 활성산소로 기능이 떨어지는 경우가 많습니다. 저희는 무기 메타물질과의 계면을 이용해 전자전달계에 인공 전자전달 경로를 만들어 미토콘드리아의 전자전달 활성을 크게 높였습니다.</p><p>플라즈모닉 메타물질의 맞춤형 대량 합성·공학과 멀티스케일 온디맨드 프린팅<br>화학공학자로서 저희는 플라즈모닉 메타물질의 대량 합성과 공학에 집중합니다. 공기-물 계면에 조립된 플라즈모닉 콜로이드 나노입자의 균일한 단일층이 플라즈모닉 나노입자를 원하는 곳에 전달하고 응용하는 훌륭한 도구가 됨을 보였습니다. 예를 들어 기계적 힘 없이 다양한 플라즈모닉 나노입자 단일층을 원하는 대로 인쇄할 수 있는 모세관 매개 역전사(capillary-mediated inverse transfer)를 제안했습니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Novel Plasmonic Sensors and Optofluidic Integrated Platforms for Innovative Diagnostics and Environmental Monitoring<br>Nanoplasmonic sensors have attracted great interest owing to their superior sensing performance. We develop novel optofluidic platforms integrated with uniform plasmonic nanostructures for various sensing applications. For example, we are working on next-generation optofluidic molecular diagnostic chips that achieve ultrafast amplification of target genes via optical polymerase chain reaction (PCR), taking advantage of the rapid light-to-heat conversion of plasmonic nanostructures. We are also interested in optofluidic sensing platforms that enable in situ, sensitive monitoring of various biological molecules in complex environments.</p><p>Artificial Biological Materials Interfaced with Inorganic Metamaterials for Biomedical Applications<br>We are interested in the rational design and synthesis of artificial biological materials that mimic, or enhance, key functions of their biological counterparts. For example, the electron transport chain (ETC) in mitochondria is essential for maintaining mitochondrial function, but it often becomes dysfunctional because of mitochondrial DNA mutations or reactive oxygen species. We have recently developed artificial electron-transfer pathways in the mitochondrial ETC by interfacing it with inorganic metamaterials, which dramatically improves ETC activity.</p><p>Tailor-Made, Large-Scale Synthesis of Plasmonic Metamaterials and On-Demand Multiscale Printing<br>As chemical engineers, we focus on the large-scale synthesis and engineering of plasmonic metamaterials. We have shown that a uniform monolayer of plasmonic colloidal nanoparticles assembled at an air–water interface is an excellent toolbox for the on-demand delivery and application of plasmonic nanoparticles. For example, we recently proposed capillarity-mediated inverse transfer, which prints monolayers of various plasmonic nanoparticles on demand without applying mechanical force.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '강태욱';

-- 조현석
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서강대학교 2005 공학사</li><li>University of South Carolina 2013 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>University of Alabama 박사후연구원 (2013–2015)</li><li>현대자동차 책임연구원 (2015–2016)</li><li>한국에너지기술연구원 선임·책임연구원 (2016–2024)</li><li>과학기술연합대학원대학교 부교수 (2022–2024)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>I. Kim, J. Choi, S. Lee, J. Park, C. Lee, J. Seo, J. Kwon, G. Doo, H. Park, D. Lee, W. Cho, C. Kim, N. V. Myung, S. Han, B. An*, M. Kim*, and H. Cho*, "Engineering MnNiPx Cathode via Dual Role of Mn: Simultaneous Enhancement of Activity and Intermittent Operation Durability," <em>Adv. Funct. Mater.</em> 36, e76622 (2026)</li><li>G. Jung, Y. Yun, S. An, D. Kim, M. Sepe, S. Choi, J. Seo, M. Kim, S. Lee, H. Park, S. Shimpalee, H. Kim, C. Lee, G. Doo*, and H. Cho*, "Versatile decal-transfer method for fabricating and analyzing microporous layers in polymer electrolyte membrane water electrolysis," <em>Small</em> 21, 2500086 (2025)</li><li>Y. Yun, J. Choi, Y. Park, H. Park, G. Doo, M. Kim, S. Han, J. Park, S. Lee, C. Lee*, and H. Cho*, "Optimizing Hybrid-phase IrO<sub>2</sub> Catalysts with Ti for Enhanced Oxygen Evolution Reaction for Proton Exchange Membrane Water Electrolysis," <em>Small</em> 21, 2503601 (2025)</li><li>M. Mehdi, B. An, H. Kim, S. Lee, C. Lee, M. Seo, M. Noh, W. Cho, C. Kim, C. Choi, B. Kim, M. Kim, and H. Cho*, "Rational Design of a Stable Fe-rich Ni-Fe Layered Double Hydroxide for the Industrially Relevant Dynamic Operation of Alkaline Water Electrolyzers," <em>Adv. Energy Mater.</em> 13, 2204403 (2023)</li><li>C. Lee, K. Shin, Y. Park, Y. Yun, M. Kim, W. Cho, C. Kim, H. Lee, S. Lee, G. Henkelman, and H. Cho*, "Catalyst-support interaction in Zr<sub>2</sub>ON<sub>2</sub>-supported IrO<sub>x</sub> electrocatalysts to break the trade-off relationship between the activity and stability in the acidic oxygen evolution reaction," <em>Adv. Funct. Mater.</em> 33, 2301557 (2023)</li></ul>$q$,
