-- 김현철
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>University of Maryland, College Park 2004 박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>미국 국립보건원(NIH) 박사후연구원 (2004–2007)</li><li>Duke University 의과대학 연구조교수 (2007–2008)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Yongho Jang, Haemin Kim, Semi Yoon, Hohyeon Lee, Jangsun Hwang, Jaehun Jung, Jin Ho Chang, Jonghoon Choi, Hyuncheol Kim, “Exosome-based photoacoustic imaging guided photodynamic and immunotherapy for the treatment of pancreatic cancer”, J Control Release 330 (2021) 293-304</li><li>Hyounkoo Han, Doyeon Kim, Yongho Jang, Minkyu Seo, Kwangmeyung Kim, Jong Bum Lee, Hyuncheol Kim, “Focused ultrasound-triggered chemo-gene therapy with multifunctional nanocomplex for enhancing therapeutic efficacy”, J Control Release 322 (2020) 346-356</li><li>Doyeon Kim, Jae Hwan Lee, Hyungwon Moon, Minkyu Seo, Hyounkoo Han, Hongkeun Yoo, Howon Seo, Jingu Lee, Sujung Hong, Pilhan Kim, Hak Jong Lee, Jin Wook Chung, Hyuncheol Kim, “Development of evaluation of an ultrasound-triggered microbubble combined transarterial chemoembolization (TACE) formulation on rabbit VX2 liver cancer model”, Theranostics 11 (2021) 79-92</li><li>Hohyeon Lee, Jieun Han, Heejun Shin, Hyounkoo Han, Kun Na, Hyuncheol Kim, “Combination of chemotherapy and photodynamic therapy for cancer treatment with sonoporation effects”, J Control Release 283 (2018) 190-199</li><li>Doyeon Kim, Suhyun Park, Hongkeun Yoo, Suhyeon Park, Jeewon Kim, Kyuhee Yum, Kwangmeyung Kim, Hyuncheol Kim, “Overcoming anticancer resistance by photodynamic therapy-related efflux pump deactivation and ultrasound-mediated improved drug delivery efficiency, Nano Converg 7 (2022) 30</li><li>Hohyeon Lee, Yongho Jang, Suhyun Park, Hyejin Jang, Eun-Joo Park, Hyun Jung Kim, Hyuncheol Kim, “ Development and evaluation of a CEACAM6-targeting theranostic nanomedicine for photoacoustic-based diagnosis and chemotherapy of metastatic cancer”, Theranostics 8 (2018) 4247-4261</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>Ph.D., University of Maryland, College Park (2004)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Postdoctoral Fellow, National Institutes of Health (2004–2007)</li><li>Research Assistant Professor, Duke University School of Medicine (2007–2008)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Yongho Jang, Haemin Kim, Semi Yoon, Hohyeon Lee, Jangsun Hwang, Jaehun Jung, Jin Ho Chang, Jonghoon Choi, Hyuncheol Kim, “Exosome-based photoacoustic imaging guided photodynamic and immunotherapy for the treatment of pancreatic cancer”, J Control Release 330 (2021) 293-304</li><li>Hyounkoo Han, Doyeon Kim, Yongho Jang, Minkyu Seo, Kwangmeyung Kim, Jong Bum Lee, Hyuncheol Kim, “Focused ultrasound-triggered chemo-gene therapy with multifunctional nanocomplex for enhancing therapeutic efficacy”, J Control Release 322 (2020) 346-356</li><li>Doyeon Kim, Jae Hwan Lee, Hyungwon Moon, Minkyu Seo, Hyounkoo Han, Hongkeun Yoo, Howon Seo, Jingu Lee, Sujung Hong, Pilhan Kim, Hak Jong Lee, Jin Wook Chung, Hyuncheol Kim, “Development of evaluation of an ultrasound-triggered microbubble combined transarterial chemoembolization (TACE) formulation on rabbit VX2 liver cancer model”, Theranostics 11 (2021) 79-92</li><li>Hohyeon Lee, Jieun Han, Heejun Shin, Hyounkoo Han, Kun Na, Hyuncheol Kim, “Combination of chemotherapy and photodynamic therapy for cancer treatment with sonoporation effects”, J Control Release 283 (2018) 190-199</li><li>Doyeon Kim, Suhyun Park, Hongkeun Yoo, Suhyeon Park, Jeewon Kim, Kyuhee Yum, Kwangmeyung Kim, Hyuncheol Kim, “Overcoming anticancer resistance by photodynamic therapy-related efflux pump deactivation and ultrasound-mediated improved drug delivery efficiency, Nano Converg 7 (2022) 30</li><li>Hohyeon Lee, Yongho Jang, Suhyun Park, Hyejin Jang, Eun-Joo Park, Hyun Jung Kim, Hyuncheol Kim, “ Development and evaluation of a CEACAM6-targeting theranostic nanomedicine for photoacoustic-based diagnosis and chemotherapy of metastatic cancer”, Theranostics 8 (2018) 4247-4261</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>유전자 전달 기능성 나노의약<br>기능성 나노의약 연구실은 siRNA, mRNA 같은 유전자 기반 치료제를 효과적으로 전달하는 나노 전달 시스템을 개발합니다. 일반적인 나노의약은 세포내 흡수(endocytosis) 효율이 낮다는 한계가 있는데, 저희는 나노의약을 세포막을 통해 직접 전달하는 「나노드릴」 기술을 개발했습니다. 이 기술은 일반 나노의약보다 훨씬 높은 전달 효율을 보이며, 이를 이용해 암과 면역 질환 치료를 위한 mRNA 백신과 siRNA 기반 기능성 나노의약을 개발하고 있습니다.</p><p>천연물 기반 기능성 나노의약: 암 면역치료와 면역 질환<br>펩타이드·단백질 등 천연 소재로 나노구조체를 개발합니다. 이 나노구조체는 천연 소재의 치료 기능은 유지하면서 독성은 크게 줄이고 안정성은 높입니다. 개발한 천연물 기반 나노의약을 암과 류마티스 관절염 같은 면역 질환 치료제로 최적화하고 있습니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Gene-Delivery Functional Nanomedicines<br>The Functional Nanomedicine Lab develops nano-delivery systems that effectively deliver gene-based therapeutics such as siRNA and mRNA. To overcome the limits of intracellular delivery of nanomedicines, such as inefficient endocytosis, we have developed a "nano-drill" technology that delivers nanomedicines directly through the cell membrane, with markedly higher delivery efficiency than conventional nanomedicines. Using this technology, we are developing mRNA vaccines and siRNA-based functional nanomedicines for cancer and immune-related diseases.</p><p>Natural-Substance-Based Functional Nanomedicines for Cancer Immunotherapy and Immune-Related Diseases<br>We develop nanostructures from peptide- and protein-based natural materials. These nanostructures retain the therapeutic functions of the natural materials while greatly reducing toxicity and improving stability. The resulting nanomedicines are being optimized as therapeutics for cancer and immune-related diseases such as rheumatoid arthritis.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '김현철';

