  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Seoul National University (1995)</li><li>Ph.D., Seoul National University (2001)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Team Leader, LG Chem Research Park (2001–2009)</li><li>Principal Investigator, Korea Research Institute of Chemical Technology (2009–2014)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Dong Hyeon Kim1,†, Hee Hwan Kim1,†, Juchan Kim1, Youngchang Byun2,*, and Kyoung-Su Ha1,*, Recovery of methyl methacrylate from waste poly (methyl methacrylate) pellets using a low-temperature plasma and zeolites, Chemical Engineering Journal, accepted, 2024. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2024.154438</li><li>Wonho Jung, Jinwon Lee*, and Kyoung-Su Ha*, A Combined Production Technology for Ethylene and Hydrogen with an Ethane Cracking Center and Dielectric Barrier Discharge Plasma Reactor, Chemical Engineering Journal 462 (2023) 142155. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2023.142155</li><li>Wonho Jung, Jinwon Lee*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Ethylene Production Processes in a Carbon-Neutral Strategy, Energy Conversion and Management, 311 (2024) 118462. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.enconman.2024.118462</li><li>Juchan Kim, Jaekwon Jeoung, Jonghyun Jeon, Jip Kim, Young Sun Mok, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Effects of dielectric particles on non-oxidative coupling of methane in a dielectric barrier discharge plasma reactor, Chemical Engineering Journal 377 (2019) 119896-119908. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2018.09.057</li><li>Daegak Kim, Gyung-Ah Park, Jemi Lim, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Effects of spatially restricted Ni nanocrystals within ordered mesopores on the production of syngas, Chemical Engineering Journal 316 (2017) 1011-1025. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cej.2017.02.014</li><li>Jongkook Hwang†, Geunjae Kwak†, Yun-Jo Lee, Yong Tae Kim, Inyoung Jeong, Seongseop Kim, Ki-Won Jun*, Kyoung-Su Ha*, Jinwoo Lee*, Direct confinement of Ru nanoparticles inside nanochannels of large pore mesoporous aluminosilicate for Fischer–Tropsch synthesis, Journal of Materials Chemistry A 3 (2015) 23725-23731. https://doi.org/10.1039/C5TA06184A</li><li>Kyoung-Su Ha*, Geunjae Kwak, Ki-Won Jun, Jongkook Hwang, Jinwoo Lee*, Ordered mesoporous carbon nanochannel reactors for high-performance Fischer–Tropsch synthesis, Chemical Communications 49 (2013) 5141-5143. https://doi.org/10.1039/C3CC00297G</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>고효율 불균일계 촉매와 소형 반응기 설계<br>졸-겔법이나 나노캐스팅으로 규칙적 메조다공성 불균일계 촉매를 제조하고 나노 크기 소재를 합성해 효율적인 불균일 촉매 시스템을 개발합니다. 실험실 규모의 고정층 반응기, 교반조 반응기 같은 기존 반응 시스템과 새로운 미세구조 반응기를 설계해 소형 화학공정 설계에 적용합니다. 효율적인 통합 화학공정 개발을 위한 반응속도론 연구도 주요 연구 분야입니다.</p><p>대체 원료 기반 연료 생산과 친환경 공정 개발<br>천연(셰일) 가스의 효율적 활용이 대체 원료로서 큰 관심을 받고 있습니다. C1 화학은 불균일계 촉매로 청정 연료와 화학제품을 만드는 중요한 방법입니다. 저희 연구실은 졸-겔, 나노캐스팅, 나노 소재 합성 같은 새로운 제조 경로로 만든 규칙적 메조다공성 촉매를 이용해 합성가스로부터 알코올, 탄화수소, 화학 중간체를 합성하는 연구를 해 왔습니다. 촉매 전환을 통해 바이오매스를 유용한 화학제품과 연료로 바꾸는 연구와, 소형 화학공정 개발을 위한 미세구조 반응기 응용도 연구합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Highly Efficient Heterogeneous Catalysts and Design of Compact Reactors<br>We prepare ordered mesoporous heterogeneous catalysts by sol–gel or nanocasting methods and synthesize nanosized materials to develop efficient heterogeneous catalytic systems. Conventional reaction systems, such as lab-scale fixed-bed and stirred-tank reactors, and novel micro-structured reactors are designed and applied toward compact chemical process design. Developing reaction kinetics is another main part of our research toward efficient integrated chemical processes.</p><p>Fuels from Alternative Feedstocks and Environmentally Benign Processes<br>The efficient utilization of natural (shale) gas as an alternative feedstock has attracted enormous interest, and C1 chemistry is an important route to clean fuels and chemicals over heterogeneous catalysts. We have investigated the synthesis of alcohols, hydrocarbons, and chemical intermediates from syngas using ordered mesoporous catalysts made by novel routes such as sol–gel, nanocasting, and nanosized material synthesis. We also study the catalytic conversion of biomass into useful chemicals and fuels, and the application of micro-structured reactors to compact chemical processes.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '하경수';

-- 나정걸
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>KAIST 화학공학과 2001 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>한국에너지기술연구원 선임·책임연구원 (2004–2016)</li><li>한국에너지기술연구원 바이오자원순환연구실장 (2013–2016)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>Eungsu Kang, Eunjoo Moon, Wooho Song, Lyul Ho Kim, Ji Sung Hyung, Jae-Hwan Jo, Jeong-Ho Park, Min-Sik Kim, Jeong-Geol Na, Yoo Seong Choi, “Chitosan/oleamide nanofluid as a significant medium for enhancing gas utilization efficiency in C1-gas microbial biotransformation”, Chemical Engineering Journal 433 (2022) 133846.</li><li>Seo Young Jo, Jina Son, Yu Jung Sohn, Seo Hyun Lim, Ji Yeon Lee, Jee in Yoo, Se Young Park, Jeong-Geol Na, Si Jae Park, “A shortcut to carbon-neutral bioplastic production: Recent advances in microbial production of polyhydroxyalkanoates from C1 resources”, International Journal of Biological Macromolecules 192 (2021) 978-998.</li><li>Tae Uk Khang, Min-Jae Kim, Jee In Yoo, Yu Jung Sohn, Sang Goo Jeon, Si Jae Park, Jeong-Geol Na, “Rapid analysis of polyhydroxyalkanoate contents and its monomer compositions by pyrolysis-gas chromatography combined with mass spectrometry (Py-GC/MS)”, International Journal of Biological Macromolecules 174 (2021) 449-456.</li><li>Diep Thi Ngoc Nguyen, Ok Kyung Lee, Chaeil Lim, Jinwon Lee, Jeong-Geol Na, Eun Yeol Lee, “Metabolic engineering of type II methanotroph, Methylosinus trichosporium OB3b, for production of 3-hydroxypropionic acid from methane via a malonyl-CoA reductase-dependent pathway”, Metabolic Engineering 59 (2020) 142-150.</li><li>Min-Sik Kim, Myounghoon Moon, Hana Nur Fitriana, Jin-Suk Lee, Jeong-Geol Na, Gwon Woo Park, “Pressurized cultivation strategies for improved microbial hydrogen production by Thermococcus onnurineus NA1”, Bioprocess and Biosystems Engineering 43 (2020) 1119-1122.</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>Ph.D., Chemical Engineering, KAIST (2001)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Senior/Principal Researcher, Korea Institute of Energy Research (2004–2016)</li><li>Head, Bioresource Recycling Laboratory, Korea Institute of Energy Research (2013–2016)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>Eungsu Kang, Eunjoo Moon, Wooho Song, Lyul Ho Kim, Ji Sung Hyung, Jae-Hwan Jo, Jeong-Ho Park, Min-Sik Kim, Jeong-Geol Na, Yoo Seong Choi, “Chitosan/oleamide nanofluid as a significant medium for enhancing gas utilization efficiency in C1-gas microbial biotransformation”, Chemical Engineering Journal 433 (2022) 133846.</li><li>Seo Young Jo, Jina Son, Yu Jung Sohn, Seo Hyun Lim, Ji Yeon Lee, Jee in Yoo, Se Young Park, Jeong-Geol Na, Si Jae Park, “A shortcut to carbon-neutral bioplastic production: Recent advances in microbial production of polyhydroxyalkanoates from C1 resources”, International Journal of Biological Macromolecules 192 (2021) 978-998.</li><li>Tae Uk Khang, Min-Jae Kim, Jee In Yoo, Yu Jung Sohn, Sang Goo Jeon, Si Jae Park, Jeong-Geol Na, “Rapid analysis of polyhydroxyalkanoate contents and its monomer compositions by pyrolysis-gas chromatography combined with mass spectrometry (Py-GC/MS)”, International Journal of Biological Macromolecules 174 (2021) 449-456.</li><li>Diep Thi Ngoc Nguyen, Ok Kyung Lee, Chaeil Lim, Jinwon Lee, Jeong-Geol Na, Eun Yeol Lee, “Metabolic engineering of type II methanotroph, Methylosinus trichosporium OB3b, for production of 3-hydroxypropionic acid from methane via a malonyl-CoA reductase-dependent pathway”, Metabolic Engineering 59 (2020) 142-150.</li><li>Min-Sik Kim, Myounghoon Moon, Hana Nur Fitriana, Jin-Suk Lee, Jeong-Geol Na, Gwon Woo Park, “Pressurized cultivation strategies for improved microbial hydrogen production by Thermococcus onnurineus NA1”, Bioprocess and Biosystems Engineering 43 (2020) 1119-1122.</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>멀티스케일 특성을 고려한 생물공정의 설계와 최적화<br>생물공정은 세포 내 대사 네트워크, 세포 간 상호작용, 생물반응기 안의 시공간적 효과가 얽힌 멀티스케일 특성을 가집니다. 이 효과들은 서로 영향을 주고받으며 결국 공정 성능을 결정합니다. 저희는 미생물 세포가 있는 생물반응기의 복잡한 거동을 분석하고, 공정의 정량적 기술을 바탕으로 새로운 시스템을 설계·최적화합니다. 세포 내 핵심 대사물질 모니터링, 배가스 분석, 반응속도 모델링, 반응기 설계, 스케일다운 연구를 수행하며, 이를 통해 「기술」로 여겨지던 미생물 발효를 생명공학의 핵심 분야로 만들고자 합니다.</p><p>탄소중립을 위한 C1 가스 전환 생물공정 개발<br>탄소중립 사회는 오늘날 인류가 마주한 중요한 과제입니다. 생촉매를 이용한 C1 가스의 생물학적 전환은 온실가스 배출을 줄이고 친환경 화학제품을 생산하는 유망한 방법입니다. 다만 기체 기질이 배양액으로 잘 녹아들지 않아 세포 안 목표 생성물로 가는 탄소 흐름이 제한되고 생산성 향상이 어렵습니다. 또한 기질(기체), 배양액(액체), 세포(고체)의 3상 거동 때문에 수학적 해석도 어렵습니다. 저희는 앞서 말한 도구들로 생물학적 가스 전환 시스템을 최적화해 탄소중립 사회 구축에 기여하고자 합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Design and Optimization of Bioprocesses with Multiscale Features<br>Bioprocesses have multiscale characteristics involving intracellular metabolic networks, cell-to-cell interactions, and spatiotemporal effects within bioreactors. These effects influence one another and ultimately determine process performance. Our objective is to analyze these complex behaviors in bioreactors with microbial cells and to design and optimize novel systems based on a quantitative description of the process. Our work includes monitoring critical intracellular metabolites, off-gas analysis, kinetic modeling, reactor design, and scale-down approaches, so that microbial fermentation, long regarded as an art, becomes a core part of biotechnology.</p><p>Bioprocess Development for C1 Gas Conversion toward a Net-Zero Future<br>A carbon-neutral society is a crucial agenda for humanity today. Amid the net-zero push, biological C1 gas conversion using biocatalysts is a promising option for mitigating greenhouse gas emissions and producing green chemicals. Yet engineering issues remain: the poor mass transfer of gaseous substrates into the culture broth limits carbon flux toward target products inside cells and restricts productivity, and the three-phase behavior of substrates (gas), medium (liquid), and cells (solid) makes mathematical analysis difficult. We optimize biological gas conversion systems with the tools above, ultimately contributing to a net-zero society.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '나정걸';

