-- 신희종
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>서울대학교 2014 공학사</li><li>서울대학교 2020 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>서울대학교 박사후연구원 (2020–2022)</li><li>Northwestern University 박사후연구원 (2023–2025)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>“Durable and Active Nitrogen-Coordinated Iron Single-Atom Catalyst for Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cells Through Carbon Encapsulation” Advanced Energy Materials 14 (2024) 2400565.</li><li>“Electrochemically generated electrophilic peroxo species accelerates alkaline oxygen evolution reaction”, Joule 7 (2023), 1902-1919.</li><li>“Supramolecular tuning of supported metal phthalocyanine catalysts for hydrogen peroxide electrosynthesis”, Nature Catalysis 6 (2023) 234-243.</li><li>“Carbon Shell on Active Nanocatalyst for Stable Electrocatalysis”, Accounts of Chemical Research 55 (2022) 1278-1289.</li><li>“Atomic-level Tuning of Co-N-C Catalyst for High-Performance Electrochemical H2O2 Production”, Nature Materials 19 (2020) 436-44.</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Seoul National University (2014)</li><li>Ph.D., Seoul National University (2020)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Postdoctoral Researcher, Seoul National University (2020–2022)</li><li>Postdoctoral Researcher, Northwestern University (2023–2025)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>“Durable and Active Nitrogen-Coordinated Iron Single-Atom Catalyst for Proton Exchange Membrane Fuel Cells Through Carbon Encapsulation” Advanced Energy Materials 14 (2024) 2400565.</li><li>“Electrochemically generated electrophilic peroxo species accelerates alkaline oxygen evolution reaction”, Joule 7 (2023), 1902-1919.</li><li>“Supramolecular tuning of supported metal phthalocyanine catalysts for hydrogen peroxide electrosynthesis”, Nature Catalysis 6 (2023) 234-243.</li><li>“Carbon Shell on Active Nanocatalyst for Stable Electrocatalysis”, Accounts of Chemical Research 55 (2022) 1278-1289.</li><li>“Atomic-level Tuning of Co-N-C Catalyst for High-Performance Electrochemical H2O2 Production”, Nature Materials 19 (2020) 436-44.</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>에너지 응용을 위한 기초 전기화학<br>에너지 변환(연료전지, 수전해, CO₂ 포집·전환, H₂O₂ 생산을 위한 전기촉매)과 에너지 저장(유기계·수계 전해질 전지)의 효율은 계면 전하 전달과 다양한 분자 상호작용을 지배하는 전기화학적 특성으로 대부분 결정됩니다. 이 기초 반응은 재생에너지 변환·저장, 화학물질·연료 생산 등 실제 응용에서 핵심 역할을 합니다. 전체 전기화학 성능은 전기촉매 소재와 반응 환경을 깊이 이해하고 전략적으로 설계하는 데 달려 있으므로, 저희는 기초 반응 메커니즘을 규명하고 그 결과를 실제 기술에 적용하는 데 함께 집중합니다.</p><p>전기화학 에너지 공학과 CO₂ 활용<br>재생 전력이 늘면서 많은 산업이 탄소 배출을 줄이기 위해 전기화로 전환하고 있지만, 기존 열화학 공정은 전기화가 어려운 경우가 많아 화학 제조 분야는 큰 도전에 직면해 있습니다. 저희는 재생 전력과 물로 화학 연료와 원료를 생산하는 전기촉매 기술을 개발합니다. 촉매 소재에 대한 기초 연구에서 출발해 전체 전해조 시스템으로 통합하고, 산업 수준의 성능 지표를 갖춘 기체확산층과 막전극접합체(MEA)를 설계합니다. 이 접근을 ① CO₂의 화학 원료·재생 연료 전환과 대기 중 탄소 포집, ② 탄화수소와 저가 원료의 고부가 화학물질 전환, ③ 효율적 에너지 응용을 위한 전기촉매와 계면 개발 등 잠재력이 큰 전기화학 경로에 적용하고자 합니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Fundamental Electrochemistry for Energy Applications<br>The efficiency of energy conversion (electrocatalysis for fuel cells, water electrolyzers, CO₂ capture and conversion, and H₂O₂ generation) and energy storage (organic- and aqueous-electrolyte batteries) is predominantly determined by electrochemical properties that regulate interfacial charge transfer and various molecular interactions. These fundamental reactions play a pivotal role in practical applications, including renewable energy conversion and storage and the production of chemicals and fuels. Because overall electrochemical performance relies on a deep understanding and strategic design of electrocatalytic materials and reaction environments, our group focuses both on elucidating fundamental reaction mechanisms and on applying our findings to real-world technologies.</p><p>Electrochemical Energy Engineering and CO₂ Utilization<br>With the increasing availability of renewable electricity, many industries are turning to electrification to reduce their carbon footprint, but chemical manufacturing faces challenges because conventional thermochemical routes are often difficult to electrify. We develop electrocatalytic technologies that produce chemical fuels and feedstocks from renewable electricity and water, from fundamental studies of catalyst materials to their integration into full electrolyzer systems, including gas diffusion layers and membrane electrode assemblies engineered to industrially relevant performance metrics. We apply this approach to promising electrochemical routes, including (1) the conversion of CO₂ into chemical feedstocks and renewable fuels, along with carbon capture from air; (2) the upgrading of hydrocarbons and low-cost feedstocks into high-value chemicals; and (3) electrocatalysts and interfaces for efficient energy applications.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '신희종';

-- 이웅
update faculty set
  bio_ko = $q$<h3>학력</h3><ul><li>Purdue University 화학공학과 2008 공학사</li><li>서울대학교 화학생물공학부 2014 공학박사</li></ul><h3>경력</h3><ul><li>한국과학기술연구원(KIST) 청정에너지연구센터 선임·책임연구원 (2017–2026)</li><li>고려대학교 에너지환경대학원 학연교수 (2023–2026)</li></ul><h3>주요 수상</h3><ul><li>KIST Young Fellow (2020–2022)</li></ul><h3>학회 활동</h3><ul><li>한국공업화학회 화학공정분과회 위원장 (2023)</li></ul><h3>주요 논문</h3><ul><li>“Reactive capture and electro-conversion of triethylamine-captured CO₂ to high-concentration formic acid”, <i>Joule</i> (2026), in press.</li><li>“Discovering the origin of catalyst performance and degradation of electrochemical CO₂ reduction through interpretable machine learning”, <i>ACS Catalysis</i> 15 (2025) 2158–2170.</li><li>“Accelerating the net-zero economy with CO₂-hydrogenated formic acid production: Process development and pilot plant demonstration”, <i>Joule</i> 8 (2024) 693–713.</li><li>“Electrochemically initiated synthesis of ethylene carbonate from CO₂”, <i>Nature Synthesis</i> 3 (2024) 846–857.</li><li>“Toward economical application of carbon capture and utilization technology with near-zero carbon emission”, <i>Nature Communications</i> 13 (2022) 7482.</li><li>“Catalyst-electrolyte interface chemistry for electrochemical CO₂ reduction”, <i>Chemical Society Reviews</i> 49 (2020) 6632–6665.</li><li>“General technoeconomic analysis for electrochemical coproduction coupling carbon dioxide reduction with organic oxidation”, <i>Nature Communications</i> 10 (2019) 5193.</li></ul>$q$,
  bio_en = $q$<h3>Education</h3><ul><li>B.S., Chemical Engineering, Purdue University (2008)</li><li>Ph.D., Chemical and Biological Engineering, Seoul National University (2014)</li></ul><h3>Experience</h3><ul><li>Senior/Principal Researcher, Clean Energy Research Center, Korea Institute of Science and Technology (KIST) (2017–2026)</li><li>Adjunct Professor, Graduate School of Energy and Environment, Korea University (2023–2026)</li></ul><h3>Selected Awards</h3><ul><li>KIST Young Fellow (2020–2022)</li></ul><h3>Professional Service</h3><ul><li>Chair, Chemical Process Division, Korean Society of Industrial and Engineering Chemistry (2023)</li></ul><h3>Selected Publications</h3><ul><li>“Reactive capture and electro-conversion of triethylamine-captured CO₂ to high-concentration formic acid”, <i>Joule</i> (2026), in press.</li><li>“Discovering the origin of catalyst performance and degradation of electrochemical CO₂ reduction through interpretable machine learning”, <i>ACS Catalysis</i> 15 (2025) 2158–2170.</li><li>“Accelerating the net-zero economy with CO₂-hydrogenated formic acid production: Process development and pilot plant demonstration”, <i>Joule</i> 8 (2024) 693–713.</li><li>“Electrochemically initiated synthesis of ethylene carbonate from CO₂”, <i>Nature Synthesis</i> 3 (2024) 846–857.</li><li>“Toward economical application of carbon capture and utilization technology with near-zero carbon emission”, <i>Nature Communications</i> 13 (2022) 7482.</li><li>“Catalyst-electrolyte interface chemistry for electrochemical CO₂ reduction”, <i>Chemical Society Reviews</i> 49 (2020) 6632–6665.</li><li>“General technoeconomic analysis for electrochemical coproduction coupling carbon dioxide reduction with organic oxidation”, <i>Nature Communications</i> 10 (2019) 5193.</li></ul>$q$,
  research_ko = $q$<p>머신러닝 기반 최적 공정 설계<br>화학공정은 공정 흐름도, 운전 조건, 용매, 촉매 등 여러 방식으로 구성할 수 있고, 각 선택은 다른 선택과 곱해져 경우의 수가 늘어납니다. 이 설계 공간은 직관으로 탐색하기에도, 하나씩 시뮬레이션하기에도 너무 큽니다. 그래서 저희는 모든 후보 설계를 담은 하나의 모델, 곧 슈퍼스트럭처로 설계 공간 전체를 표현하고 머신러닝으로 탐색합니다. 최적화 과정에서는 대리 모델이 엄밀한 시뮬레이션을 대신하고, 베이지안 최적화와 능동 학습이 다음 실험을 고르며, 신경망 스크리닝이 수십억 개의 후보 분자를 몇 개로 좁힙니다. 공정, 용매, 촉매를 차례로가 아니라 함께 설계해, 훨씬 적은 실험으로 최적점에 도달합니다.</p><p>미시반응속도 모델링과 멀티스케일 반응기 설계<br>공정 모델은 그 밑의 화학만큼만 정확하기에, 저희는 가장 아래에서 시작합니다. 소반응 단계로 미시반응속도(microkinetic) 모델을 세우고, 이를 반응기 전산유체역학(CFD)으로, 다시 공정 흐름도로, 마지막으로 경제성과 전과정평가(LCA)로 이어 활성화 에너지에서 톤당 생산 비용까지 끊김 없이 연결합니다. 이 연결고리를 CO₂ 수소화를 통한 포름산·메탄올 생산, 피셔–트롭시 마이크로채널 반응기, 전기화학적 CO₂ 환원 셀에 구축했습니다. 반대 방향으로도 활용해, 설명 가능한 AI로 전기화학 실험 데이터를 해석해 촉매 활성과 열화를 지배하는 인자를 찾고, 이를 전극과 반응기 설계에 바로 반영합니다.</p><p>탄소 포집·활용과 청정에너지 시스템<br>실험실의 반응이 비용 경쟁력을 갖추게 하는 것은 시스템 문제이며, 저희는 이를 끝까지 다룹니다. 계산과 실험으로 포집 용매를 모델링·선별하고, CO₂를 바로 전환해 에너지 소모가 큰 재생 단계를 생략하는 반응성 포집(reactive capture)을 연구합니다. 포름산, 메탄올, 일산화탄소, 올레핀을 만드는 전기화학·열촉매 경로를 개발하고, 기술경제성 분석과 전과정평가로 어떤 경로를 스케일업할지 판단합니다. 이 가운데 여러 연구가 파일럿 규모 실증과 산업체 기술이전에 이르렀습니다.</p>$q$,
  research_en = $q$<p>Machine Learning-Aided Optimal Process Design<br>A chemical process can be built in a number of ways — flowsheet layout, operating conditions, solvent, catalyst — and every choice multiplies the others. The space is far too large to search by intuition, and far too large to simulate one case at a time. We therefore write the whole space down as a superstructure: one model that contains every candidate design, and search it with machine learning. Surrogate models replace rigorous simulations inside the optimization loop; Bayesian optimization and active learning pick the next experiment to run; neural screening narrows a billion candidate molecules to a few. Process, solvent and catalyst are designed together rather than one after another, and an experimental campaign reaches the optimum in a fraction of the runs.</p><p>Microkinetic Modeling and Multiscale Reactor Design<br>A process model is only as good as the chemistry beneath it, so we start at the bottom. We build microkinetic models from elementary reaction steps and carry them into computational fluid dynamics of the reactor, then into the flowsheet, and finally into economics and life cycle assessment — one unbroken chain from an activation barrier to a production cost per ton. We have built it for CO₂ hydrogenation to formic acid and methanol, for Fischer–Tropsch microchannel reactors, and for electrochemical CO₂ reduction cells. We also run the chain backwards: explainable AI reads experimental electrochemical data and tells us which descriptors govern catalyst activity and degradation, and those descriptors go straight back into electrode and reactor design.</p><p>Carbon Capture, Utilization and Clean Energy Systems<br>Making a laboratory reaction compete on cost is a systems problem, and we take it the whole way. We model and screen capture solvents by computation and by experiment, and study reactive capture, which converts CO₂ directly and skips the energy-intensive regeneration step. We develop electrochemical and thermocatalytic routes to formic acid, methanol, carbon monoxide and olefins; techno-economic and life cycle assessment then decides which routes deserve to be scaled. Several of these lines have reached pilot-scale demonstration and technology transfer to industry.</p>$q$
where name_ko = '이웅';

select name_ko, length(bio_ko) bio_ko, length(bio_en) bio_en, length(research_ko) res_ko, length(research_en) res_en from faculty where published and not is_emeritus order by sort_order;